{"seq":1,"mint":"C19","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":false,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"the shown-count is not one of them","clause_quoted":true,"facts":[],"why":"The displayed grep output is partitioned into per-file matches, and the derived count `files` is stored in the Search label. Thus a count of the displayed/matched files is recoverable from the ledger.","quoted":false,"rejected_span":"        printed.push_str(&stdout);\n        printed.push_str(&format!(\"({note})\\n\"));\n        let mut by_file: std::collections::BTreeMap<String, Vec<String>> = std::collections::BTreeMap::new();\n        for line in stdout.lines() {\n            if let Some((file, rest)) = line.split_once(':') {\n                by_file.entry(file.to_string()).or_default().push(rest.to_string());\n            }\n        }\n        // One whole-search record beside the per-file hits. Without it a\n        // search that matched says only which files it hit, and where it\n        // was rooted — the thing a census turns on — is unrecoverable.\n        // Its marker comes from the search root, exactly as the\n        // zero-match record's always has.\n        let m = world.for_path(root_path);\n        let files = by_file.len();\n        buf.push(PendingEntry {\n            captured_at: workspace::now_unix(),\n            kind: ObservationKind::Search,\n            key: search_key(root_path, &m.root),\n            label: format!(\n                \"search: {root} (grep: {pattern}) — {files} file{} matched — {note}\",\n                if files == 1 { \"\" } else { \"s\" }\n            ),\n            output: String::new(),\n        });"},{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"how much the author was shown is unrecoverable from the ledger after the fact","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F2","F22","F27","F31"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"        printed.push_str(&stdout);\n        printed.push_str(&format!(\"({note})\\n\"));\n        let mut by_file: std::collections::BTreeMap<String, Vec<String>> = std::collections::BTreeMap::new();\n        for line in stdout.lines() {\n            if let Some((file, rest)) = line.split_once(':') {\n                by_file.entry(file.to_string()).or_default().push(rest.to_string());\n            }\n        }\n        // One whole-search record beside the per-file hits. Without it a\n        // search that matched says only which files it hit, and where it\n        // was rooted — the thing a census turns on — is unrecoverable.\n        // Its marker comes from the search root, exactly as the\n        // zero-match record's always has.\n        let m = world.for_path(root_path);\n        let files = by_file.len();\n        buf.push(PendingEntry {\n            captured_at: workspace::now_unix(),\n            kind: ObservationKind::Search,\n            key: search_key(root_path, &m.root),\n            label: format!(\n                \"search: {root} (grep: {pattern}) — {files} file{} matched — {note}\",\n                if files == 1 { \"\" } else { \"s\" }\n            ),\n            output: String::new(),\n            world_root: m.root,\n            world_state: m.state,\n            pattern: pattern.to_string(),\n        });\n        for (file, matches) in by_file {\n            let m = world.for_path(Path::new(&file));\n            buf.push(PendingEntry {\n                captured_at: workspace::now_unix(),\n                kind: ObservationKind::GrepMatch,\n                key: resolve_key(Path::new(&file)),\n                label: format!(\"{file} (grep: {pattern})\"),\n                output: matches.join(\"\\n\"),","why":"The complete grep stdout is appended to the printed result, each stdout line is grouped into per-file matches, and those matches are stored as per-file output. The amount shown can therefore be recovered by counting the stored lines.","quoted":true}],"at":1790113267,"cost":0.02210592,"elapsed_ms":141178,"attempts":3,"not_ve